# Architecture-Tracked Project: {{projectName}}

This project uses a living architecture document, `{{architectureFile}}`. You — the AI coding agent (Codex, OpenCode, Copilot, or any AGENTS.md-aware tool) — are responsible for keeping it in sync with the code.

> **arkive is installed.** MCP server available via `npx @ericjdz/arkive serve --stdio`. Use MCP tools when connected; edit `{{architectureFile}}` directly when not.

## Rules

1. **On every session start**: Read `{{architectureFile}}` first. It is your cross-session memory.
2. **Before any major change**: Re-read `{{architectureFile}}`.
3. **After any major change**: Update `{{architectureFile}}` and append a `history` entry.

## Major Changes

Add/remove a service, database, or external API · change communication protocols · modify infrastructure · adopt a new framework · refactor module boundaries.

## How to Update

**MCP tools (preferred):** `update_architecture`, `record_decision`, `check_drift`
**Fallback:** Edit `{{architectureFile}}` directly — add services/connections/decisions/dataFlows, append history, update `project.lastUpdated`.

## Schema (compact)

- **Service**: `{ id, name, type, technology, description, dependencies[] }`
  - `type`: `frontend | backend | database | cache | queue | gateway | cdn | storage | auth | search | monitoring | other`
- **Connection**: `{ from, to, protocol, description }`
- **Decision**: `{ id, topic, decision, rationale, alternatives[{name, whyNot}], timestamp, relatedServices[] }`
  - MUST include at least one rejected alternative with `whyNot`
- **DataFlow**: `{ name, steps[{actor, action}] }`
- **History entry**: `{ timestamp, action, summary }`

## Validation Rules

- Every `connection.from`/`to` must reference an existing `service.id`.
- Every `service.dependencies[]` entry must reference an existing `service.id`.
- Every decision must include at least one rejected alternative with `whyNot`.
- All timestamps are ISO 8601.
- Update `project.lastUpdated` on every change.

## CLI Commands

- `npx @ericjdz/arkive serve` — MCP server + web viewer
- `npx @ericjdz/arkive serve --stdio` — MCP server only (agent integration)
- `npx @ericjdz/arkive status` — architecture health check
- `npx @ericjdz/arkive reconcile` — detect drift
- `npx @ericjdz/arkive export <format>` — export (markdown, mermaid, png, svg)
- `npx @ericjdz/arkive learn` — web viewer in Learning Mode
